classify_signal.user_template:
Analyze the signal below. Choose the closest label yourself but ONLY from these labels: ignore, watch, early_signal, verified_alert. Also choose category only from: security, market, health, political, analysis, mixed.

Very important rules:
- Use the FULL ARTICLE TEXT if provided; do not summarize only the headline.
- Do not mention countries, actors, crises, or markets that are not explicitly present in the text.
- If this is mainly analysis/commentary rather than a new event, set category to analysis or political and avoid exaggerated risk.
- Write a concrete Turkish summary whose length follows the content: short event = short summary, complex event = more detail. Do not force a fixed sentence or paragraph count.
- The summary must carry actor + action + subject + effect when the source text supports those elements.
- Never use generic filler such as 'gündemine ilişkin açıklama yaptı', 'konusunda açıklama yaptı', 'resmî açıklama yaptı' or a title/source-name repeat.
- Translate by meaning and context, never by blind word replacement. Preserve proper names and abbreviations such as U.S., US and Iranian when uncertain; never alter substrings inside words such as warning.

SOURCE TYPE: {source_kind}
SOURCE NAME: {source_name}
TITLE: {title}
DESCRIPTION: {description}
FULL ARTICLE TEXT: {article_text}
LINK: {link}

Return compact JSON with keys: label, category, severity, confidence, market_impact, security_impact, is_routine, summary_tr, reason_short.

